message: "If you use this work, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "C2CS: Code to Common Semantics"
abstract: >-
  C2CS is an open, in-progress standard for describing what software does —
  its operations, data, resources, and effects — as machine-readable semantic
  documents (contracts, assessments, verdicts) whose declared behavior can be
  checked against observed behavior. It is designed as a semantic complement
  to the SBOM. The research core explores whether Large Language Models can
  infer high-level program semantics well enough to improve security
  decisions and least-privilege policy generation, deriving policy from
  inferred high-level intent rather than from observed low-level behavior.
type: software
